+## Update the user documentation with AI
+
+```bash
+pnpm docs:update_by_ai
+```
+
+A coding agent writes all the user documentation of the public website, in the folder `packages/auxiliary/website_public/docs/documentation`. No person edits a generated page by hand. The command does a full check every time: the coding agent compares all the pages with all the rules in `docs/agents_rules/user_interface`, with the glossary, and with the code. A new feature gets a section, a changed feature gets its section changed, and a removed feature loses its section.
+
+The file `.last_documented_commit` in the documentation folder holds the last documented commit. The merged pull requests, the fixed issues, and the diff of the rules since that commit are only hints that say which sections to look at first. On the first run the file does not exist, so there are no hints.
+
+The writer prompt asks for numbered task steps that explain how to find each control and what result to expect. Pages explain unfamiliar terms, use the same names throughout, and link to useful next steps instead of repeating other pages. Details and solutions must be supported by the sources.
+
+The command reads Git history, runs the coding agent, and runs the tests and the build of the website. Generated pages, sidebar changes, and the last documented commit file remain local and uncommitted. Existing local changes are allowed. The command never stages files, creates or switches branches, writes commits, pushes, merges, or creates a pull request or merge request. The developer handles those actions and publication outside this process.
+
+| Command | Effect |
+| --- | --- |
+| `pnpm docs:update_by_ai` | Generates and checks the documentation; leaves the files uncommitted. |
+| `pnpm docs:update_by_ai --dry-run` | Prints the prompt with the hints. Nothing changes, and no coding agent runs. |
+| `pnpm docs:update_by_ai --agent claude` | Uses `claude` in place of `codex`, the default. |
+| `pnpm docs:update_by_ai --verbose` | Shows what the coding agent does while it works. |
+| `pnpm docs:update_by_ai --model <name> --effort <level>` | Chooses the model and the effort level of the coding agent. Without them, the coding agent uses its own settings. |
+| `pnpm docs:update_by_ai --only <rule file>` | A small trial: checks only the features of these rule files. The file `.last_documented_commit` is not written. |
+
+The writer reuses verified screenshots supplied in `packages/auxiliary/website_public/docs/public/documentation_images`, with descriptive alternative text, near the matching steps or controls. Screenshot metadata records the application source and the state shown. The writer does not invent screenshots or image paths.
+
+To score the quality of the generated pages, run `pnpm docs:judge_by_ai`. It prints a table of scores from 1 to 5 for each page, and the worst problems of each page. It edits no file. The judge uses contract version 3 and defaults to Claude `claude-sonnet-5-5` with `high` effort. Every deduction requires evidence and a matching severity. `--only` excludes unselected pages from scoring. Reports record scope and settings; blocking findings prevent acceptance regardless of the average. Verification limitations require review. Compare only runs with the same contract and unchanged inputs.
+
+Every generated page has the mark `<!-- generated by docs:update_by_ai -->`, and every section names its rule file in a comment `<!-- source: <path> -->`. The page `shortcuts.md` stays generated by `pnpm docs:shortcuts`.
+
